{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep, etc.</b> The reason it was necessary to state this verse once again, although He already said so in parashat Acharei Mot (Leviticus 18:26), is to say that one must keep the commandments so that they not be violated — whether by the people themselves or by others — and thereby the land will not vomit you out. From this you learn that if the commandments are not kept, the land will vomit out even those who keep them, because they did not protest against those who did not keep them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:55.064169238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}